# Configuration contract for a future explicitly approved release.
# Both features remain disabled until that release is authorized.
# This is a preparation template, NOT a runnable post-migration configuration.
# After the security migrations, STAFF_SECURITY_ENABLED must be true before
# serving authentication; disabling only STAFF_DASHBOARD_ENABLED is containment.
STAFF_SECURITY_ENABLED=false
STAFF_DASHBOARD_ENABLED=false
# Required when enabling the dashboard in production: up to 200 positive IDs.
STAFF_DASHBOARD_USER_IDS=
# Provision JWT_SECRET, SESSION_SECRET and STAFF_ACCESS_SIGNING_SECRET independently
# in the secret manager (at least 32 bytes each). Match the staff key to the DB key.
# Do not rely on the deployed session-secret fallback; fence session invalidation
# when provisioning the currently absent SESSION_SECRET under change approval.
# Preserve the existing 32-byte base64 APP_ENC_KEY for existing authenticators.
# Runtime uses chatforia_dev. Migration/recovery credentials stay outside the app.
# DATABASE_URL is supplied only from the restricted runtime secret store.
# The proposed dedicated-user systemd unit reads /etc/chatforia/api-runtime.env
# as root and injects the values into a non-root Node process. The unit sets
# DOTENV_CONFIG_PATH=/dev/null; omit both DOTENV_CONFIG_PATH and
# DOTENV_CONFIG_OVERRIDE from the EnvironmentFile so it cannot override the
# unit setting or revive the legacy dotenv load. Do not inherit the root PM2
# saved doadmin URL.
# Require TLS peer identity with the verified provider CA/hostname; do not copy
# the existing doadmin URL or leave sslmode=require as unverified transport.
# STAFF_EXPECTED_DATABASE=defaultdb for the inspected target; verify independently.
# SESSION_SECRET= (independent random >=32 bytes; required by production startup)
